WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.947
Sovereignty summary.

00:00:01.897 --> 00:00:04.079
Sovereign in name only.

00:00:04.079 --> 00:00:10.318
This page brings together eight dimensions of sovereignty failure documented across the TENET5 investigation.

00:00:10.318 --> 00:00:26.693
Canada cannot make its own medicine, cannot patrol its own Arctic, cannot sell its oil to alternative markets, cannot store its data on domestic servers, cannot equip its military, cannot manufacture semiconductors, cannot control its food prices, and cannot hold its own government accountable through democratic institutions.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:30.159
Each failure is documented from official government data.

00:00:30.159 --> 00:00:35.738
Together they describe a country that claims sovereignty but cannot exercise it in any meaningful sense.

00:00:35.738 --> 00:00:37.704
The sovereignty test.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:52.965
A sovereign nation can: make its own essential goods, patrol its own borders, sell its exports to alternative markets, control its own data, equip and deploy its military, feed its population without concentrated dependence, and hold its government accountable through democratic institutions.

00:00:52.965 --> 00:00:55.397
Canada fails every test.

00:00:55.397 --> 00:00:57.579
This is not accidental.

00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:02.738
Each sovereignty failure is the product of policy choices made by captured institutions.

00:01:02.738 --> 00:01:06.329
Pipeline politics eliminated energy alternatives.

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:09.749
Procurement failures degraded military capability.

00:01:09.749 --> 00:01:12.522
Offshoring eliminated manufacturing.

00:01:12.522 --> 00:01:14.931
Cloud adoption surrendered data.

00:01:14.931 --> 00:01:18.897
The captured democratic system ensures these failures persist.

00:01:18.897 --> 00:01:21.499
Sovereignty requires capability.

00:01:21.499 --> 00:01:25.602
Capability requires institutions that serve the public interest.

00:01:25.602 --> 00:01:28.034
The institutions are captured.

00:01:28.034 --> 00:01:30.079
Sovereignty is fiction.
